  "rationale": "Every exfiltrate step needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold there, which needs stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin needs admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need a foothold on dc or adfs plus stolen_admin. stolen_admin can only come from kerberoasting, which needs a foothold on appserver or apiserver. That foothold needs reach_internal and stolen_user. The shortest chain is: 1 phish_workstation (gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user), 2 pivot_internal, 3 auth_appserver, 4 kerberoast_dc, 5 auth_dc, 6 escalate_dc, 7 dump_dbadmin_dc, 8 auth_db, 9 escalate_db, 10 exfiltrate_db. Every step is required by a later step, and no technique sets two of the needed variables at once (except phishing, already used), so 10 is the minimum."
